<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistan Feb consumer prices up 11.1 pct yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Pakistan Feb consumer prices up 11.1 pct yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>ISLAMABAD 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's consumer price index rose 11.1 percent in February year-on-year, compared to 13.4 percent in January and 9.76 percent in February 1996, the Federal Bureau of Statistics said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The index, using 1990/91 as base year, rose 1.09 percent to 194.2 in February from 192.11 in January. The index stood at 170.6 in February 1996.</p>
<p>					 Feb	  Jan	   Feb 96</p>
<p>CONSUMER PRICE  base 1990/91   194.20     192.11	170.60</p>
<p>    Month-on-month		  +1.09	+2.17	 +0.70</p>
<p>    Year-on-year		   +11.10     +13.40	+ 9.76</p>
<p>-- Islamabad newsroom 9251-274757</p>
</text>
